libdtfl -- thanks

	libdtfl exists because of the design and the working code of the
	timely and differential dataflow projects.  The port follows their
	structure closely, and the correctness core keeps their names,
	comments, and algorithm constants.  Thanks to Frank McSherry and to
	everyone who has contributed to:

		timely dataflow
		differential dataflow
		the timely diagnostics tools

	The queue between worker threads is a port of the Rust standard
	library's mpsc list channel, which comes from crossbeam-channel;
	thanks to the Crossbeam and Rust developers.

	And thanks to the authors of the hegel property-testing engine,
	used for the library's property tests.
